---

### `.gitignore`

This covers Node.js / ServiceNow SDK (`@servicenow/sdk`) artifacts, VS Code workspace clutter, OS files, and—most importantly—credential files so you never accidentally push PDI passwords, OAuth tokens, or API keys.

```gitignore
# Environment variables & ServiceNow credentials
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.key
*.pem
*credentials*.json
*secrets*.json
.now-auth*

# ServiceNow SDK / Fluent build artifacts
dist/
target/
.now/
now-build/

# Node.js / Package Managers
node_modules/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
.pnpm-store/

# Logs & Exports (e.g., XML Update Set exports, CSV/Excel table dumps)
*.log
*.xml.bak
exports/
tmp/

# IDE & Editor
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
!.vscode/settings.json
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# OS & WSL2
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
Desktop.ini
*:Zone.Identifier